  "summary": "CLOSEDQUORUM is a 16.4MB 64-bit Go Windows implant whose command and control is delegated to a quorum of commercial LLM providers (DeepSeek, Qwen, Mistral, Gemini), which vote on each next action (inject, persist, steal, move) via plurality voting. It steals LSASS credentials, browser passwords and crypto wallets, exfiltrating AES-256-GCM/base64 data to an operator Discord webhook, and evades analysis with ETW patching, time-based guards and WindowsUpdate-themed persistence. The public distribution build is inert, with placeholder API keys and webhook, and configured per-operator builds are generated at compile time.",
